    "short": "Pulie Badze Wildlife Sanctuary is located in Kohima District of Nagaland.",
    "description": "Pulie Badze Wildlife Sanctuary is located in Kohima District of Nagaland. It was first designated as a protected area in 1980. The park is named after the 2,296-metre (7,533 ft) mountain Pulie Badze, which means \"Pulie's Seat\", named after the legendary folktale character \"Pulie\". The park is home to a vast variety of birds like Tragopan Blythii (the state bird of Nagaland), White-naped Yuhina and Dark-rumped swift.",
